# CaseLinker persistent identifiers for perma-id/w3id.org
#
# Submit this file as `caselinker/.htaccess` in
# https://github.com/perma-id/w3id.org (PR against their main).
# Rules match the path *after* `/caselinker/`, so
#   https://w3id.org/caselinker/resource/case/{id}
# becomes a 303 to
#   https://caselinker.up.railway.app/resource/case/{id}
#
# 303 See Other keeps the path (httpRange-14): the w3id IRI names the
# resource; the Railway URL returns a description. Do not use 302 — that
# drops the path onto `/patterns` today.
#
# Targets the app must serve (already in run/main.py + run/deref.py):
#   GET /resource/{path}     case, agency, platform, location, provenance graph
#   GET /ns/provenance       provenance vocabulary (HTML or Turtle)
#
# Content negotiation on those routes: HTML for browsers; Accept
# text/turtle or application/ld+json for clients. CORS is open for GET.
#
# After the host leaves Railway, change only the target host below.
# Re-submit the same relative rules to perma-id.

Header set Access-Control-Allow-Origin *
Header set Access-Control-Allow-Headers "Accept, Authorization, Content-Type"
Header set Access-Control-Allow-Methods "GET, HEAD, OPTIONS"

RewriteEngine on
RewriteRule ^$ https://caselinker.up.railway.app/ [R=303,L]
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://caselinker.up.railway.app/$1 [R=303,L,QSA]
